# Fastlane environment variables — local development template.
#
# Copy to .env and fill in your values:
#   cp fastlane/.env.default fastlane/.env
#
# .env is gitignored and should never be committed.
# In CI, these are set via GitHub Actions secrets.
#
# EVERY KEY HERE IS COMMENTED OUT, AND MUST STAY THAT WAY.
#
# fastlane auto-loads this file (Fastlane::Helper::DotenvHelper — it loads
# `.env` and `.env.default` from the first of [fastlane/, its parent] holding
# any *.env* file). A bare `KEY=` does not leave the key unset: it exports an
# empty string, and "" is truthy in Ruby, so every `ENV[...] ||` check treats
# it as configured.
#
# That is not hypothetical. `MATCH_GIT_BASIC_AUTHORIZATION=` made match run
#
#     git clone … -c http.extraheader='Authorization: Basic '
#     remote: invalid credentials
#
# on a machine whose `gh` credential helper could clone the repo perfectly
# well — the empty header overrode working authentication. `MATCH_PASSWORD=`
# is the same trap one step later: match stops prompting and tries to decrypt
# with an empty passphrase.
#
# The Appfile already carries an `env_or` helper written to survive this file.
# Commenting the keys out fixes it at the source instead.

# App Store Connect API Key
# Generate at: https://appstoreconnect.apple.com/access/integrations/api
# APPLE_API_KEY_ID=
# APPLE_API_ISSUER_ID=
# Base64 of the .p8: `cat AuthKey_XXXX.p8 | openssl base64 -A`. Locally you can
# skip it and set APPLE_API_KEY_FILEPATH to the .p8 instead; CI needs this one.
# APPLE_API_KEY_P8=
# APPLE_API_KEY_FILEPATH=

# Match — code signing certificate storage
# Repo: https://github.com/Spooky-Labs/spooktacular-certificates
# MATCH_PASSWORD=
# Base64 of `<gh-user>:<PAT>`. Leave unset to use your normal git credentials
# (e.g. the `gh` credential helper) — setting it empty breaks them.
# MATCH_GIT_BASIC_AUTHORIZATION=

# Optional: installer certificate identity for productbuild
# INSTALLER_CERT_NAME="3rd Party Mac Developer Installer: ..."

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# App Store metadata — developer contact fields
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fastlane reads these for `upload_to_app_store`, `upload_to_testflight`,
# and `deliver` lanes. If you fork Spooktacular and submit under your
# own Apple developer account, copy to `.env` and replace — the Fastfile
# reads the env vars and falls back to sensible placeholders.

# FASTLANE_TEAM_ID=
# FASTLANE_ITC_TEAM_ID=
# FASTLANE_APPLE_ID=
# FASTLANE_CONTACT_FIRST_NAME=
# FASTLANE_CONTACT_LAST_NAME=
# `FASTLANE_SUPPORT_EMAIL` is the single knob for the
# customer-facing inbox. Fastfile cascades it into
# `CONTACT_EMAIL`, `APP_REVIEW_EMAIL`, and `APP_FEEDBACK_EMAIL`
# unless those are overridden individually.
# FASTLANE_SUPPORT_EMAIL=
# FASTLANE_CONTACT_EMAIL=
# FASTLANE_CONTACT_PHONE=
# FASTLANE_APP_REVIEW_EMAIL=
# FASTLANE_APP_FEEDBACK_EMAIL=
